#
# The trap is that the observed anisotropy is NOT the pixel aspect. Pixel aspect is
# diag(fx, fy): it acts along the image axes and can produce no skew at all. The 25 Hz flight's
# anisotropy sits 35 degrees off any image axis, and the two flights agree on its magnitude
# (1.0079, 1.0085) while disagreeing 36 degrees on its axis — which a camera property cannot
# do and a tag on a differently-sloped surface can. So this is the bound on what could still be
